  "body": "## Problem and change\n\nA closed STEP solid can have a spline face that ends at a pole. The old deviation measure can reject its valid mesh.\n\n`mesh_pole::settle` moves the free parameter at a pole to the mean of the other two triangle corners. It uses one side of the period. It keeps the move only when the surface point stays within 1e-9 mm. `mesh_deviation::face` applies this step before it samples a spline triangle. Analytic faces keep their existing path. The deviation bounds do not change.\n\nThe PR includes two original fixtures:\n\n- `testdata/models/sphere_quarter_pole.step`: a quarter sphere, R 25, with a rational B-spline dome and an apex pole.\n- `testdata/models/q02_3d_mold.step`: the recorded SolidCraft QA part from #3034. The file has 347101 bytes. SHA256: `111862a3c03262db764d92e63c5c32f384541b14840d494f6bf3bf4fc5bb9567`.\n\nBoth fixtures have STEP agreement rows and named tests. No HSMWorks source or assets were used.\n\n## Cause and readings\n\nThe issue reports an open mesh on v0.24.0. On upstream/main `8be100737`, the import itself refused q02:\n\n```text\nsolid #3738 'Mould' could not be tessellated: machining mesh: face Some(10) stands 5.089e-1 mm off its surface, tolerance 5e-3 mm\n```\n\nFace 10 is the ellipsoid boss (`#3666`), with a pole at its top. Its mesh sag is about 0.004 mm. The old measure interpolated the free parameter across half the period. Its projection hint was then on the far side of the surface. A finer chord did not reduce the measured bound.\n\nWith the fix, the recorded q02 file imports with 48780 facets and no open edges. Its signed volume is 97163.50 mm^3. SolidCraft reports 97165.69 mm^3. The test allows 10 mm^3.\n\nThe slice at z = 19.6875, the reported height, has area 1382.27 mm^2. Slices at z = 18.5, 20, 25 and 29 also close. The test checks the measured areas within 0.5 mm^2.\n\n## Regression pins\n\n- Kernel `mesh_deviation_pole::a_fan_at_a_spline_pole_measures_by_its_true_sag`.\n- Kernel `mesh_deviation_pole::a_solid_with_a_spline_pole_meshes_inside_the_tolerance`.\n- App `import_step_spline_pole::a_solid_with_a_spline_pole_imports_closed_and_slices`.\n- Kernel lib `mesh_pole::tests` (3 tests).\n- App `import_step_q02_mold::the_recorded_q02_mould_imports_closed_and_slices_at_the_reported_height`.\n- App `import_step_q02_mold::the_recorded_q02_mould_generates_a_3d_flat_finish` (heavy lane).\n\nThe q02 generation pin uses the full recorded model and the normal undoable generation command. It uses Flat Finish3D, BN-0600, top z = 30 mm, bottom z = 18 mm, stepover 2 mm, and tolerance 0.05 mm. It checks finite moves and more than 10 mm of horizontal Feed on the base at z = 18 mm. The initial release run passed: 1 test, 8.27 s. The final-head heavy run also passed this pin: 1 test, 7.90 s.\n\nMutation check on this follow-up:\n\n- Restored `mesh_deviation.rs` from upstream/main: RED, exit 101, in 5.19 s. The new q02 generation pin refused the import with the original diagnostic:\n\n```text\nsolid #3738 'Mould' could not be tessellated: machining mesh: face Some(10) stands 5.089e-1 mm off its surface, tolerance 5e-3 mm\n```\n\n- Restored the fix byte for byte: GREEN, 1 test passed in 7.88 s. The restored file has no diff.\n\n## Final-head validation\n\nHead: `d3df8a0256a5b768c0d21e4034acf0c0f8c34fd4`.\nBase: upstream/main `6e1805bfdae52fcfea71a946d381dfbfdefc79f5`.\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: GREEN, exit 0. All 91 steps passed in 22.6 minutes. Tests: 2214 passed, 0 failed, 32 ignored. The q02 generation pin is in the heavy lane. The direct release run above passed it.\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main`: GREEN, exit 0. All 253 reached steps completed in 55.9 minutes. No unexpected step failed. Tests: 105 passed, 6 tracked expected failures, 0 ignored. Kernel: 4 passed. Motion: 57 passed and 2 expected failures. App: 44 passed and 4 expected failures.\n- `cargo clippy -j 8 -p camcraft-kernel -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: GREEN, exit 0, in 1 minute 21 seconds.\n\nThe gate accepts the six tracked expected failures below. They are not passing tests.\n\n| Crate | Test | Tracked issue |\n|---|---|---|\n| motion | `ring_tests::the_stock_ring_level_reaches_the_air_planner_with_the_stock` | #1950 |\n| motion | `ring_tests::the_stock_ring_level_plans_adaptive_with_no_budget_note` | #1950 |\n| app | `pocket3d_hsm::the_users_whole_model_bore_roughs_adaptive_on_each_level` | #1950 |\n| app | `lead_approach::an_axis_aligned_lead_start_posts_the_users_arc_entry_as_g18_or_g19` | #2849 |\n| app | `lead_approach::the_horizontal_arc_entry_on_the_users_pocket_verifies_silent` | #2849 |\n| app | `shoulder_adaptive::fig8_outside_containment_with_em0800_and_clearing_kinds_works` | #2849 |\n\n## Limits\n\nThe 3D generation pin covers a Flat finish of the base at z = 18 mm. It keeps the full recorded model. Earlier broad Waterline and Parallel attempts did not finish. They are not passing generation results. The PR does not claim that all 3D strategies complete on q02.\n\nThe 1e-9 mm point check in `settle` has no separate pin. No constructed surface has a zero derivative at a point that is not a pole.\n\nNo goldens or UI source changed. No screenshots are required for this diff.\n\nChangelog: A closed STEP solid with a spline face that ends in a pole (for example an ellipsoid or a dome from SolidCraft) now imports. Before, the import refused it with \"stands ... mm off its surface\".\n\nFixes #3034\n",
